From: alpha-liu-01 <116528196+alpha-liu-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:24:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] drm/msm/dsi: send the refresh-rate command on the first
 frame

dsi_refresh_flag starts at 60, meaning "the panel runs at 60 Hz". With
continuous splash the bootloader leaves the panel in its 120 Hz setting
and dsi_panel_enable() is skipped, so a first frame at 60 Hz never sent
DISP_BC_60HZ and the panel flickered. Start the flag at 0 (unknown), so
the first frame always sends the command for its rate.
---
 techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c
index d95a7ab17..3d49b0c80 100644
--- a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c
@@ -3675,7 +3675,13 @@ struct dsi_panel *dsi_panel_get(struct device *parent,
 	drm_panel_init(&panel->drm_panel);
 	panel->drm_panel.dev = &panel->mipi_device.dev;
 	panel->mipi_device.dev.of_node = of_node;
-	panel->dsi_refresh_flag = 60;
+	/*
+	 * Unknown until a refresh-rate command (DISP_BC_*HZ) has been sent.
+	 * With continuous splash the bootloader leaves the panel in its 120 Hz
+	 * setting and dsi_panel_enable() is skipped; starting at 60 meant a
+	 * first frame at 60 Hz never sent DISP_BC_60HZ, and the panel flickered.
+	 */
+	panel->dsi_refresh_flag = 0;
 
 	rc = drm_panel_add(&panel->drm_panel);
 	if (rc)
